{
  "requirement": "When source-access policy denies a path that a model tool call names\nexplicitly, the harness MUST return a tool error naming the path and the reason\nit cannot be read, add no evidence input, and continue the assessment.\nDiscovery and search MUST leave denied candidates out of their entries,\nreporting untracked ones under {cite}`requirements.authoring.not_listed`. Malformed tool\narguments and ordinary read failures MUST also return explanatory tool errors.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate. I did not request implementation source, because the supplied tests and their assertions were enough to map every obligation.\n\n**Obligations derived from `requirements.authoring.read_denial`:**\n1. An explicitly named path that policy denies produces a tool error that names the path and the reason.\n2. A denial adds no evidence input, and the assessment continues.\n3. Discovery and search leave denied candidates out of their entries. Untracked candidates are reported under `not_listed`, which is cited context (`requirements.authoring.not_listed`) and not reassessed here.\n4. Malformed tool arguments return explanatory tool errors.\n5. Ordinary read failures return explanatory tool errors. They are distinct from denials.\n\n**Coverage of the error that names path and reason, across denial causes and tools:**\n- Generated `evidence/`, including symlink aliases and `./` forms: `tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[generated_evidence_is_excluded_from_reads_search_and_discovery]`. It covers `habeas`, `list_files`, `ripgrep` and `ast_grep`. It asserts `PermissionDenied`, the path, and \"generated evidence\".\n- Workspace disallow rules: `tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[allowed_ignored_and_external_sources_are_discoverable_but_disallowed_descendants_are_not]`, `tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[cargo_output_is_discovered_and_read_without_building_or_allowing_other_target_files]` and `tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs]`. They assert the path and \"disallowed\" across all tools.\n- Symlinks leaving the project: `tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requests_through_symlinks_leaving_the_project_are_denials]` and `mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[a_read_through_a_symlink_leaving_the_project_returns_an_error_to_the_model]`.\n- Untracked paths: `tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[untracked_diagnostics_name_git_add_and_an_allow_rule]` asserts the path, `git add`, and the allow rule.\n- Policy resolution (alias targets, disallowed ancestors, `..` components): the `access.rs` tests. They assert `PermissionDenied`, and the ancestor test also asserts the path is in the message.\n\n**Coverage of \"add no evidence input and continue the assessment\":**\n- `mod.rs#...a_read_through_a_symlink_leaving_the_project_returns_an_error_to_the_model` asserts that a second request is made, that the error text is delivered to the model, that the secret contents are not delivered, and that the file is absent from the evidence.\n- `tests/authoring_batch.rs#fn[a_denied_read_returns_an_error_and_its_assessment_continues]` asserts that the denied subject made two requests and every assessment completed. It also asserts that `tool_failures.habeas == 1` and that the denied file is not recorded.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[explicit_untracked_reads_return_an_untracked_error_and_the_assessment_continues]` covers all four tools end to end. It asserts two requests, the `git add` guidance, no leaked content, and a completed outcome.\n- The tools tests assert `recorded_inputs().is_empty()` after denials.\n\n**Coverage of denied candidates left out of discovery and search:**\n- `git_tools_allow_staged_and_dirty_sources_but_hide_untracked_files` and `git_symlink_reads_require_both_the_alias_and_target_to_be_tracked` check that untracked entries are absent.\n- The evidence test checks that `evidence/` is absent from listings, from `ripgrep` matches and from `ast_grep` matches.\n- The disallow test checks that `generated/private` descendants are absent from search results.\n- `listings_and_searches_name_untracked_files_without_their_contents` checks that a disallowed `secret.rs` and `evidence/note.txt` are absent from `not_listed` and from entries. It also checks that untracked files are named without their contents.\n\n**Coverage of malformed arguments:**\n- `mod.rs#...malformed_and_failed_reads_return_to_the_model_and_the_assessment_continues` covers malformed `habeas` arguments and checks that the error is delivered to the model.\n- The `ripgrep`, `ast_grep`, `outline`, `list_files`, `references`, `github` and `next_page` argument errors are asserted by message in the tools tests and in `pages.rs`.\n\n**Coverage of ordinary read failures:**\n- The `habeas` missing-file, absent-item and out-of-range cases are in the `mod.rs` test above. That test also asserts that the failure kind is not `PermissionDenied`.\n- Build-output requests are in `requests_for_book_or_target_output_are_ordinary_read_failures`.\n- OS permission failures are in `operating_system_permission_failures_are_ordinary_read_failures`.\n- A listing of a missing path or of a file is in `failed_listings_return_explanatory_tool_errors`.\n- A request outside the project is in `unpermitted_requests_outside_the_project_are_recoverable_tool_errors`.\n\nThe sub-requirements `read_denial.mandatory`, `read_denial.untracked` and `read_denial.build_output` refine the subject, and their own tests carry them. I found no obligation of the subject text that is untested or asserted wrongly.",
  "references": "b0affe935af59f6c42ef8c8e6412ebdda687c10177f666be25eccd9049b7a335",
